  "output": "## Test Coverage Analysis — `canon/web`\n\n**Headline finding: there is no test infrastructure at all.** `package.json` has no `test` script, no `vitest`/`jest`/`@testing-library/*` in `devDependencies`, and the only `*.test.*` files in the tree live in `node_modules`. Everything below is a gap in the sense that *zero* of it is covered.\n\nGiven Next.js 16 + React 19 + no existing runner, I'd recommend **Vitest** (native ESM/TS, fast, no babel config fights with the App Router) plus `@testing-library/react` for the handful of components with real logic. Setup skeleton first, then gaps grouped as requested.\n\n### 0. Infrastructure setup (blocking gap)\n\n```ts\n// vitest.config.ts\nimport { defineConfig } from \"vitest/config\";\nimport react from \"@vitejs/plugin-react\";\nimport path from \"path\";\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [react()],\n  test: {\n    environment: \"jsdom\",\n    setupFiles: [\"./vitest.setup.ts\"],\n    exclude: [\"node_modules\", \".next\"],\n  },\n  resolve: { alias: { \"@\": path.resolve(__dirname, \".\") } },\n});\n```\n```json\n// package.json additions\n\"scripts\": { \"test\": \"vitest run\", \"test:watch\": \"vitest\" },\n\"devDependencies\": {\n  \"vitest\": \"^2\", \"@vitejs/plugin-react\": \"^4\",\n  \"@testing-library/react\": \"^16\", \"@testing-library/jest-dom\": \"^6\", \"jsdom\": \"^25\"\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 1. Untested pure functions (no mocking needed — highest ROI, do these first)\n\n**`lib/cn.ts::cn()`**\n```ts\n// lib/cn.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { cn } from \"@/lib/cn\";\n\ndescribe(\"cn\", () => {\n  it(\"merges plain class strings\", () => {\n    expect(cn(\"px-2\", \"text-g-900\")).toBe(\"px-2 text-g-900\");\n  });\n  it(\"dedupes conflicting tailwind classes, last wins\", () => {\n    expect(cn(\"px-2\", \"px-4\")).toBe(\"px-4\");\n  });\n  it(\"drops falsy values\", () => {\n    expect(cn(\"px-2\", false, undefined, null, \"\")).toBe(\"px-2\");\n  });\n  it(\"handles conditional object syntax\", () => {\n    expect(cn({ \"text-g-900\": true, \"text-g-500\": false })).toBe(\"text-g-900\");\n  });\n});\n```\n\n**`types/rules.ts::ruleSpecificity()`** — this is the function that decides which survivorship rule wins, so it's the single most business-critical untested function in the repo.\n```ts\n// types/rules.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { ruleSpecificity, survivorshipRuleSchema } from \"@/types/rules\";\n\ndescribe(\"ruleSpecificity\", () => {\n  const base = { id: \"1\", strategy: \"escalate\" as const, description: \"d\" };\n  it(\"both wildcard scores 0\", () => {\n    expect(ruleSpecificity({ ...base, field: \"*\", entityType: \"*\" })).toBe(0);\n  });\n  it(\"field-only specific scores 2\", () => {\n    expect(ruleSpecificity({ ...base, field: \"name\", entityType: \"*\" })).toBe(2);\n  });\n  it(\"entityType-only specific scores 1\", () => {\n    expect(ruleSpecificity({ ...base, field: \"*\", entityType: \"account\" })).toBe(1);\n  });\n  it(\"both specific scores 3 (highest)\", () => {\n    expect(ruleSpecificity({ ...base, field: \"name\", entityType: \"account\" })).toBe(3);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"survivorshipRuleSchema refine\", () => {\n  const base = { id: \"1\", field: \"*\", entityType: \"*\", description: \"d\" };\n  it(\"rejects prefer_source without preferredSourceId\", () => {\n    const r = survivorshipRuleSchema.safeParse({ ...base, strategy: \"prefer_source\" });\n    expect(r.success).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"accepts prefer_source with preferredSourceId\", () => {\n    const r = survivorshipRuleSchema.safeParse({\n      ...base, strategy: \"prefer_source\", preferredSourceId: \"src-1\",\n    });\n    expect(r.success).toBe(true);\n  });\n  it(\"accepts most_recent/most_complete/escalate without preferredSourceId\", () => {\n    for (const strategy of [\"most_recent\", \"most_complete\", \"escalate\"] as const) {\n      expect(survivorshipRuleSchema.safeParse({ ...base, strategy }).success).toBe(true);\n    }\n  });\n});\n```\n\n**Zod schemas across `types/*.ts`** — these are the wire contract with the Python engine (comments literally say \"mirrors engine/pipeline/schema.py\"), so a schema regression is a cross-service break with no other safety net.\n```ts\n// types/source.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { createSourceSchema, sourceConfigSchema } from \"@/types/source\";\n\ndescribe(\"sourceConfigSchema\", () => {\n  it(\"rejects empty objects array\", () => {\n    expect(sourceConfigSchema.safeParse({ objects: [] }).success).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"accepts optional filter omitted\", () => {\n    expect(sourceConfigSchema.safeParse({ objects: [\"Account\"] }).success).toBe(true);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"createSourceSchema\", () => {\n  it(\"rejects empty name\", () => {\n    expect(createSourceSchema.safeParse({ name: \"\", kind: \"salesforce\", config: { objects: [\"a\"] } }).success).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"rejects name over 80 chars\", () => {\n    const name = \"a\".repeat(81);\n    expect(createSourceSchema.safeParse({ name, kind: \"salesforce\", config: { objects: [\"a\"] } }).success).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"accepts name at exactly 80 chars (boundary)\", () => {\n    const name = \"a\".repeat(80);\n    expect(createSourceSchema.safeParse({ name, kind: \"salesforce\", config: { objects: [\"a\"] } }).success).toBe(true);\n  });\n  it(\"rejects unknown kind\", () => {\n    expect(createSourceSchema.safeParse({ name: \"x\", kind: \"oracle\", config: { objects: [\"a\"] } }).success).toBe(false);\n  });\n});\n```\n```ts\n// types/conflict.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { severitySchema } from \"@/types/conflict\";\n\ndescribe(\"severitySchema\", () => {\n  it.each([1, 2, 3, 4])(\"accepts valid severity %i\", (v) => {\n    expect(severitySchema.safeParse(v).success).toBe(true);\n  });\n  it.each([0, 5, 1.5, -1])(\"rejects invalid severity %s\", (v) => {\n    expect(severitySchema.safeParse(v).success).toBe(false);\n  });\n});\n```\n```ts\n// types/resolution.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { reviewActionSchema } from \"@/types/resolution\";\n\ndescribe(\"reviewActionSchema\", () => {\n  it(\"accepts approve/reject with no extra fields\", () => {\n    expect(reviewActionSchema.safeParse({ action: \"approve\" }).success).toBe(true);\n    expect(reviewActionSchema.safeParse({ action: \"reject\" }).success).toBe(true);\n  });\n  it(\"rejects override without overrideValue\", () => {\n    expect(reviewActionSchema.safeParse({ action: \"override\" }).success).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"rejects override with empty overrideValue\", () => {\n    expect(reviewActionSchema.safeParse({ action: \"override\", overrideValue: \"\" }).success).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"rejects a reviewedBy field even if the client sends one (must be server-derived)\", () => {\n    const r = reviewActionSchema.safeParse({ action: \"approve\", reviewedBy: \"spoofed\" });\n    // discriminatedUnion strips/ignores unknown keys by default — assert that,\n    // don't assume it silently trusts client-supplied identity.\n    expect(r.success && !(\"reviewedBy\" in r.data)).toBe(true);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Untested server functions — edge cases & missing error handling\n\n**`lib/server/sources.ts`** — two real bugs-in-waiting here worth calling out specifically:\n- `listSources()` calls `sourceSchema.parse(row)` (not `safeParse`) with **no try/catch anywhere in the call chain**. One malformed DB row (e.g. a `config` that predates a schema change) throws an unhandled `ZodError` straight out of a Server Component.\n- `countSourcesBySide()` never counts `\"synthetic\"` sources into `crm` or `warehouse` — only into its own bucket. `get-started/page.tsx` sums all three to decide \"configured\", so this happens to work today, but nothing tests that a synthetic-only setup still shows \"Continue to sources\" instead of \"Add your first source.\"\n\n```ts\n// lib/server/sources.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi, beforeEach } from \"vitest\";\n\nvi.mock(\"@/lib/db\", () => ({ getDb: vi.fn() }));\nvi.mock(\"next/server\", () => ({ connection: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(undefined) }));\n\nimport { getDb } from \"@/lib/db\";\nimport { listSources, countSourcesBySide } from \"@/lib/server/sources\";\n\nfunction mockRows(rows: unknown[]) {\n  (getDb as any).mockReturnValue({\n    select: () => ({ from: () => ({ orderBy: () => Promise.resolve(rows) }) }),\n  });\n}\n\ndescribe(\"listSources\", () => {\n  it(\"returns an empty array when there are no rows\", async () => {\n    mockRows([]);\n    expect(await listSources()).toEqual([]);\n  });\n  it(\"parses valid rows into Source objects\", async () => {\n    mockRows([{ id: \"...\", name: \"SFDC\", kind: \"salesforce\", config: { objects: [\"Account\"] }, createdAt: new Date() }]);\n    const result = await listSources();\n    expect(result).toHaveLength(1);\n  });\n  it(\"throws (does not silently drop) a row that fails schema validation\", async () => {\n    mockRows([{ id: \"not-a-uuid\", name: \"bad\", kind: \"salesforce\", config: {}, createdAt: new Date() }]);\n    await expect(listSources()).rejects.toThrow();\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"countSourcesBySide\", () => {\n  it(\"buckets salesforce/hubspot as crm, databricks/snowflake as warehouse\", async () => {\n    mockRows([\n      { id: \"1\", name: \"a\", kind: \"salesforce\", config: { objects: [\"x\"] }, createdAt: new Date() },\n      { id: \"2\", name: \"b\", kind: \"snowflake\", config: { objects: [\"x\"] }, createdAt: new Date() },\n    ]);\n    expect(await countSourcesBySide()).toEqual({ crm: 1, warehouse: 1, synthetic: 0 });\n  });\n  it(\"counts synthetic sources only under `synthetic`, not crm/warehouse — document this explicitly\", async () => {\n    mockRows([{ id: \"1\", name: \"s\", kind: \"synthetic\", config: { objects: [\"x\"] }, createdAt: new Date() }]);\n    expect(await countSourcesBySide()).toEqual({ crm: 0, warehouse: 0, synthetic: 1 });\n  });\n});\n```\n\n**`lib/server/auth.ts`** — the label fallback chain (`username → email → userId`) and the throw-on-no-session path are both unguarded.\n```ts\n// lib/server/auth.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi } from \"vitest\";\n\nvi.mock(\"@clerk/nextjs/server\", () => ({ auth: vi.fn(), currentUser: vi.fn() }));\nimport { auth, currentUser } from \"@clerk/nextjs/server\";\nimport { requireReviewer, getReviewer } from \"@/lib/server/auth\";\n\ndescribe(\"requireReviewer\", () => {\n  it(\"throws when isAuthenticated is false\", async () => {\n    (auth as any).mockResolvedValue({ isAuthenticated: false, userId: null });\n    await expect(requireReviewer()).rejects.toThrow(/no authenticated reviewer/i);\n  });\n  it(\"throws when isAuthenticated is true but userId is missing (inconsistent session)\", async () => {\n    (auth as any).mockResolvedValue({ isAuthenticated: true, userId: null });\n    await expect(requireReviewer()).rejects.toThrow();\n  });\n  it(\"prefers username over email over userId\", async () => {\n    (auth as any).mockResolvedValue({ isAuthenticated: true, userId: \"u1\" });\n    (currentUser as any).mockResolvedValue({ username: \"j.rao\", primaryEmailAddress: { emailAddress: \"j@x.com\" } });\n    expect((await requireReviewer()).label).toBe(\"j.rao\");\n  });\n  it(\"falls back to email when username is null\", async () => {\n    (auth as any).mockResolvedValue({ isAuthenticated: true, userId: \"u1\" });\n    (currentUser as any).mockResolvedValue({ username: null, primaryEmailAddress: { emailAddress: \"j@x.com\" } });\n    expect((await requireReviewer()).label).toBe(\"j@x.com\");\n  });\n  it(\"falls back to userId when username and email are both absent\", async () => {\n    (auth as any).mockResolvedValue({ isAuthenticated: true, userId: \"u1\" });\n    (currentUser as any).mockResolvedValue({ username: null, primaryEmailAddress: null });\n    expect((await requireReviewer()).label).toBe(\"u1\");\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"getReviewer\", () => {\n  it(\"returns null when signed out instead of throwing\", async () => {\n    (auth as any).mockResolvedValue({ isAuthenticated: false });\n    expect(await getReviewer()).toBeNull();\n  });\n  it(\"delegates to requireReviewer when signed in\", async () => {\n    (auth as any).mockResolvedValue({ isAuthenticated: true, userId: \"u1\" });\n    (currentUser as any).mockResolvedValue({ username: \"j.rao\" });\n    expect(await getReviewer()).toEqual({ userId: \"u1\", label: \"j.rao\" });\n  });\n});\n```\n\n**`lib/db/index.ts::getDb()`** — untested error path + untested caching behavior.\n```ts\n// lib/db/index.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect, beforeEach, vi } from \"vitest\";\n\ndescribe(\"getDb\", () => {\n  beforeEach(() => {\n    vi.resetModules();\n    delete (globalThis as any).canonDb;\n    delete (globalThis as any).canonSql;\n    delete process.env.DATABASE_URL;\n  });\n\n  it(\"throws an actionable error when DATABASE_URL is unset\", async () => {\n    const { getDb } = await import(\"@/lib/db\");\n    expect(() => getDb()).toThrow(/DATABASE_URL is not set/);\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns the same cached instance across calls (HMR-safety)\", async () => {\n    process.env.DATABASE_URL = \"postgres://user:pass@localhost:5432/db\";\n    const { getDb } = await import(\"@/lib/db\");\n    expect(getDb()).toBe(getDb());\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Untested middleware — access-control gap\n\n`proxy.ts` is the *only* thing standing between an unauthenticated request and a console that \"renders a company's full org chart\" (per its own comment). It has zero coverage.\n```ts\n// proxy.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\n// createRouteMatcher is exported by @clerk/nextjs/server; re-derive the matcher\n// logic here or export `isPublicRoute` from proxy.ts for direct testing.\nimport { createRouteMatcher } from \"@clerk/nextjs/server\";\n\nconst isPublicRoute = createRouteMatcher([\"/\", \"/sign-in(.*)\", \"/sign-up(.*)\"]);\n\ndescribe(\"isPublicRoute\", () => {\n  it.each([\"/\", \"/sign-in\", \"/sign-in/factor-one\", \"/sign-up\"])(\n    \"treats %s as public\",\n    (path) => expect(isPublicRoute({ url: `http://x${path}`, nextUrl: { pathname: path } } as any)).toBe(true),\n  );\n  it.each([\"/sources\", \"/runs\", \"/conflicts/123\", \"/api/sources\"])(\n    \"treats %s as protected\",\n    (path) => expect(isPublicRoute({ url: `http://x${path}`, nextUrl: { pathname: path } } as any)).toBe(false),\n  );\n});\n```\nAlso untested: the `config.matcher` regex itself — no test asserts that a static asset (`.svg`, `.woff2`) actually bypasses the middleware, or that `/api/*` and `/trpc/*` are covered. That regex is exactly the kind of thing that silently breaks on refactor.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Component logic gaps\n\nMost components are pure markup, but a few have branching worth testing:\n\n```ts\n// components/console/nav-rail.test.tsx\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi } from \"vitest\";\nimport { render, screen } from \"@testing-library/react\";\n\nvi.mock(\"next/navigation\", () => ({ usePathname: vi.fn() }));\nvi.mock(\"@clerk/nextjs\", () => ({ UserButton: () => null }));\nimport { usePathname } from \"next/navigation\";\nimport { NavRail } from \"@/components/console/nav-rail\";\n\ndescribe(\"NavRail active state\", () => {\n  it(\"marks the matching top-level route active via aria-current\", () => {\n    (usePathname as any).mockReturnValue(\"/sources\");\n    render(<NavRail />);\n    expect(screen.getByRole(\"link\", { name: \"Sources\" })).toHaveAttribute(\"aria-current\", \"page\");\n  });\n  it(\"treats a nested route as active on its parent (startsWith)\", () => {\n    (usePathname as any).mockReturnValue(\"/conflicts/abc-123\");\n    render(<NavRail />);\n    expect(screen.getByRole(\"link\", { name: \"Conflicts\" })).toHaveAttribute(\"aria-current\", \"page\");\n  });\n  it(\"does not mark any item active on an unrelated route\", () => {\n    (usePathname as any).mockReturnValue(\"/settings\");\n    render(<NavRail />);\n    for (const link of screen.getAllByRole(\"link\"))\n      expect(link).not.toHaveAttribute(\"aria-current\");\n  });\n});\n```\n\n```ts\n// components/severity-mark.test.tsx\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { render, screen } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport { SeverityMark } from \"@/components/severity-mark\";\n\ndescribe(\"SeverityMark\", () => {\n  it.each([1, 2, 3, 4] as const)(\"always renders the label alongside the mark for severity %i\", (sev) => {\n    render(<SeverityMark severity={sev} />);\n    // AGENTS.md constraint: \"the mark alone is never the only signal\" —\n    // this is a design-system guard, not just a render smoke test.\n    expect(screen.getByText(/structural|attribute|cosmetic/i)).toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n});\n```\n\n```ts\n// components/ui/button.test.tsx\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { render, screen } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport { Button } from \"@/components/ui/button\";\n\ndescribe(\"Button\", () => {\n  it(\"defaults to primary/md variant classes\", () => {\n    render(<Button>Go</Button>);\n    expect(screen.getByRole(\"button\")).toHaveClass(\"bg-g-900\");\n  });\n  it(\"renders as the child element when asChild is set (Slot)\", () => {\n    render(<Button asChild><a href=\"/x\">Go</a></Button>);\n    expect(screen.getByRole(\"link\")).toHaveClass(\"bg-g-900\");\n  });\n  it(\"disables pointer events and lowers opacity when disabled\", () => {\n    render(<Button disabled>Go</Button>);\n    expect(screen.getByRole(\"button\")).toBeDisabled();\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. Integration test gaps\n\n- **`app/(console)/sources/page.tsx`**: no test exercises the empty-state vs. table branch based on `listSources()`'s return value — this is exactly the kind of Server Component logic that's cheap to test now and expensive to debug later once it's wired to a real DB.\n- **`app/get-started/page.tsx`**: no test confirms the CTA text switches (\"Add your first source\" vs \"Continue to sources\") based on `countSourcesBySide()` — and this is the function with the synthetic-bucket edge case above, so the two gaps compound.\n- **Auth flow end-to-end**: no test confirms that `proxy.ts`'s route protection and `requireReviewer()`'s throw actually agree — `auth.ts`'s own comment says reaching the throw \"should fail loudly rather than write an anonymous row to audit_log,\" but nothing verifies the two modules stay in sync as routes are added.\n- **Engine contract types** (`types/run.ts` — `engineStartRunRequestSchema`, `engineRunStatusSchema`): no client code exists yet to call the engine, so there's nothing to integration-test today, but flagging now because these schemas are the entire cross-service contract and will need a contract test (or a shared schema fixture) the moment a fetch call is added.\n- **Design-system guard**: `lib/clerk-appearance.ts` hardcodes hex literals specifically to keep Clerk's UI achromatic (AGENTS.md's \"no hue anywhere\" rule). Nothing asserts that — a regression test that greps `clerkAppearance.variables` for non-gray hex values would catch an accidental color creeping back in.\n\n```ts\n// app/(console)/sources/page.test.tsx (sketch — Server Components need care under RTL)\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi } from \"vitest\";\nvi.mock(\"@/lib/server/sources\", () => ({ listSources: vi.fn() }));\nimport { listSources } from \"@/lib/server/sources\";\nimport SourcesPage from \"@/app/(console)/sources/page\";\n\ndescribe(\"SourcesPage\", () => {\n  it(\"renders the empty state when there are no sources\", async () => {\n    (listSources as any).mockResolvedValue([]);\n    const jsx = await SourcesPage();\n    // assert SourcesEmptyState markup, e.g. \"No sources yet\"\n  });\n  it(\"renders the table and a count in the header when sources exist\", async () => {\n    (listSources as any).mockResolvedValue([{ id: \"1\", name: \"SFDC\", kind: \"salesforce\", config: { objects: [\"Account\"] }, createdAt: new Date() }]);\n    const jsx = await SourcesPage();\n    // assert SourceTable markup + \"1 configured\" meta text\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### Priority order if picking a starting point\n1. Zod schemas + `ruleSpecificity` (pure, zero setup, protects the engine contract).\n2. `lib/server/auth.ts` + `proxy.ts` (protects the actual security boundary).\n3. `lib/server/sources.ts` (fixes the two edge cases flagged above before they bite).\n4. Component/page tests once the first three establish the mocking patterns.\n\nWant me to actually scaffold the Vitest setup and the first batch of these test files in the repo?\n",
